# UST.G3BQ Correction Full Recursive Return Theorem v1

## Result

Start with the exact G3BM `42706 x 248` ambient first-return matrix for the G3BI correction direction at `(p,gamma)=(11,3)`. Apply the frozen original-Jacobian coordinate solver, retain every selected preimage coordinate, take the exact Griffiths-Dwork divergence with factor `1/4`, solve the resulting H11 ambient source, take the next divergence with factor `1/3`, and solve the terminal H20 ambient source.

Every one of the 248 columns reconstructs with zero residual at each stage. The three quotient blocks are

```text
H02 return          248 x 248    56,032 nonzero entries
H11 lower return   1013 x 248   228,594 nonzero entries
H20 lower return    248 x 248    55,847 nonzero entries
```

Their ordered vertical concatenation is an exact `1509 x 248` correction-source block over GF(11), with 340,473 nonzero entries and rank 248. The retained H20 image preimage lies in the already certified terminal-divergence-zero class, so the finite recursive return stops there.

## Significance

G3BQ closes the complete finite recursive return for the *selected G3BI correction source*. Earlier corpus machinery established the algorithm and executed it for a former source; G3BQ binds that machinery to the new G3BI/G3BK/G3BM data and recomputes all three stages. It therefore removes the correction-specific GF(11) H02/H11/H20 return from the live frontier.

## Exact scope

This is an exact selected-good-fiber result. It does not promote the H11 or H02 inverse action to `Q(gamma)`, compute integral monodromy along the G3BJ arc, emit terminal B89 coordinates, or decide the final 248-row physical readout.

